  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 AM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nHigh pressure will remain in control of our weather pattern through \nlate next week, meaning a continuation of warm and dry conditions. \nTemperatures will continue to run above climatological norms with \npeak warmth occurring on Sunday as the ridge amplifies over the\nregion. Daytime temperatures on Sunday will run around 10 \ndegrees above normal with valley locations warming into the low \nto mid-80s. High resolution models indicate a shortwave feature \nworking through Monday and Monday night, along with very weak \nmoisture signals working through the ridge. This could mean very\nslight chances for precipitation across southeast Idaho, \nalthough confidence remains low at this time. Otherwise, our \nnext chance of precipitation looks to be next Saturday when the \nnext trough works through.",
